# SLES layer 01: host packages, only what the desktop core runs outside a user
# shell (compositor binds, the Quickshell shell, user services, root helpers).
# Installed with transactional-update only when the next boot lacks them.
# CLI/TUI tools are NOT here: they come from mise (mise-tools.toml, userland).
# Fallback terminal (works even when userland is broken). The default terminal is
# Ghostty from userland (layer 03); xdg-terminal-exec also comes from userland,
# since SLES's 2024 snapshot lacks --dir/--print-id (see host.remove)
foot
# Wayland helpers used by binds, screenshots, OSD and the clipboard
wl-clipboard
wtype
grim
slurp
brightnessctl
pamixer
playerctl
alsa-utils
# Used by Omarchy scripts everywhere, also from root helpers and services
jq
git-core
unzip
libnotify-tools
# Automounting removable drives (Omarchy autostarts `udiskie --automount`; it
# talks to the host's udisks2 over the system bus)
udiskie
# Secrets for browsers and apps (Omarchy's choice; KDE's kwallet stays for Plasma)
gnome-keyring
secret-tool
